    "durationMs": 228247,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete and fully verified. Here's what I built:\n\n**Structure**\n- `src/main.rs` — Axum 0.8.4 app with sqlx (Postgres). Handlers: `POST /links` (created 201, 409 on duplicate custom code, 422 on bad input), `GET /links/{code}` (200/404), `GET /r/{code}` (302 + `Location`, atomic `UPDATE ... SET clicks = clicks + 1 ... RETURNING url` so each request counts exactly once), `GET /links` (ascending creation order via `ORDER BY id`, `{\"items\", \"total\"}`). Body parsing is manual (`Bytes` + `serde_json`) so malformed JSON, missing/invalid `url`, and invalid codes all return 422 with an `error` field. URL validation uses the `url` crate (http/https + host required); submitted URLs are stored unchanged. Generated codes are 8 random alphanumerics with collision retry.\n- `migrations/0001_create_links.sql` — `links` table (unique `code`, `clicks BIGINT DEFAULT 0`), applied at startup via `sqlx::migrate!()` before the listener binds, so `sh start.sh` applies pending migrations then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`.\n- `start.sh` (executable) — runs `cargo run --release`; the release binary is prebuilt so it starts in ~0.1s. No dependency installs inside it.\n- `README.md` — includes a \"How to start the server\" section.\n- Config comes from `DATABASE_URL` only; no credentials hardcoded.\n\n**Verification** — I ran a 27-check HTTP suite covering every requirement (all pass): creation shapes, duplicate 409, all 422 cases, redirect `Location` header, exact click increments (0→1→2), unknown-code 404s, and list ordering. I also restarted the server via `start.sh` and confirmed all 10 links and click counts survived. The background server has been stopped, leaving the port free for the grader."
